{
 "thread": "3w9JhJcKe9Q",
 "subject": "When imperfect detection is not so imperfect, is that ok to use just the mean + Confidence Interval?",
 "messages_listed": 3,
 "last_activity": "2017-06-26T18:49:57Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "6cOmTRkxAgAJ",
   "from": "Márcio Fernandes",
   "author": "b6d0cf10447ab522",
   "date": "2017-06-26T13:19:00Z",
   "subject": "When imperfect detection is not so imperfect, is that ok to use just the mean + Confidence Interval?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear collegues,<div><br></div><div>I am very new in the world of imperfect detection modeling, but I am really amazed by what someone can do with this powerful tool.</div><div><br></div><div>I am now trying to apply the unmarked package to deal with imperfect detection in my dataset. I have 56 sites in which I made 2-3 replicates. I used the pcount function because I believe that&#39;s my case and then I manged to correct several different taxa for imperfect detection.</div><div><br></div><div>However, some of then presented really low values of detection, so for those I got stuck in the problem of finding the appropriate boundary. Moreover, if i try to use the ranef function to see the corrected abundances I recieve many NaN (not a number) outcomes.</div><div>I see this as an ongoing challenge in the development of more appropriate equations to handle those low values, but I am also would like to question the necessity of correcting something which does seem to be well detected.</div><div><br></div><div>Then because of my problem I also have a doubt: If the detection bias is low does it mean it is ok to not consider a imperfect detection? Is it ok for those well detected taxa if I just use the mean + 95%CI for estimate the abundance in the site?</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "CaetBZ2NAQAJ",
   "from": "Márcio Fernandes",
   "author": "b6d0cf10447ab522",
   "date": "2017-06-26T14:39:29Z",
   "subject": "Re: When imperfect detection is not so imperfect, is that ok to use just the mean + Confidence Interval?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div><br></div>As I did not provide a reproducible example I will add more details about my modeling:<div><br></div><div>First I tested a full model but Hessian was singular</div><div><br></div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">fm &lt;- pcount(~read.num ~ Land_use..3. + M.O.g.dm3 + pH.CaCl2 + Log..P.mg.dm3 +K.mg.dm3 + Mg.mg.dm3 + Ca.mg.dm3 + Areia.total + Argila + D.SOLO.0.20, tax_unmark, mixture=&quot;NB&quot;)</blockquote><div><br></div><div>A reduced model also generates the Hessian singular error and using starting values did not help:</div><div><br></div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">fm.start &lt;- pcount(~read.num ~ Land_use..3.,tax_unmark, mixture=&quot;NB&quot;, starts = c(79.4,-68.6,-64.6,345.5,-66.5,-66.5,0,-3.36,10.79,-1.47))</blockquote></div><div><br></div><div>Increasing the K helps ranef to produce less NaN outcomes, but it is too computational intensive and it seems to require really large values of K (beyond hundreads of thousands)</div><div><br></div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">fm &lt;- pcount(~read.num ~ Land_use..3., bact_list_unmark$Acidobacteria_Acidobacteria, mixture=&quot;NB&quot;, se=FALSE, K = 100000) #Ten thousand<br>fm.1m &lt;- pcount(~read.num ~ Land_use..3. , bact_list_unmark_un$Acidobacteria_Acidobacteria, mixture=&quot;NB&quot;, se=FALSE, K = 1000000) # A million<br></blockquote></div><div><br></div><div>here is the outcome of ranef for each model:</div><div><br></div><div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\" class=\"gmail_quote\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">unmarked::ranef(fm)\r\n</span></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\" class=\"gmail_quote\">      Mean Mode      2.5% 97.5%<br> [1,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br> [2,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br> [3,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br> [4,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br> [5,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br> [6,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br> [7,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br> [8,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br> [9,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[10,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[11,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[12,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[13,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[14,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[15,] 5234 5234      5234 5234 <br>[16,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[17,] 2621 2621      2621 2621 <br>[18,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[19,] 1274 1274      1274 1274 <br>[20,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[21,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[22,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[23,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[24,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[25,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[26,] 865  865       865  865  <br>[27,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[28,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[29,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[30,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[31,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[32,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[33,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[34,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[35,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[36,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[37,] 1387 1387      1387 1387 <br>[38,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[39,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[40,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[41,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[42,] 3886 3886      3886 3886 <br>[43,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[44,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[45,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[46,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[47,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[48,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[49,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[50,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[51,] 7534 7534      7534 7534 <br>[52,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[53,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[54,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[55,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA   <br>[56,] NaN  Integer,0 NA   NA <br></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\" class=\"gmail_quote\"><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">unmarked::ranef(fm.1m)\r\n</span></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\" class=\"gmail_quote\">      Mean     Mode      2.5%  97.5%<br> [1,] 14872.67 14869     14438 15314<br> [2,] 20905.3  20904     20576 21237<br> [3,] NaN      Integer,0 NA    NA   <br> [4,] 18221.3  18218     17729 18720<br> [5,] 50.61943 50        48    54   <br> [6,] 10257.52 10256     10020 10499<br> [7,] NaN      Integer,0 NA    NA   <br> [8,] 16856.61 16853     16365 17356<br> [9,] NaN      Integer,0 NA    NA   <br>[10,] NaN      Integer,0 NA    NA   <br>[11,] 12104.38 12103     11859 12353<br>[12,] 18187.09 18183     17690 18691<br>[13,] 17709.57 17707     17341 18082<br>[14,] 39574.21 39570     38823 40333<br>[15,] 16823.46 16821     16458 17194<br>[16,] NaN      Integer,0 NA    NA   <br>[17,] 9313.511 9313      9173  9456 <br>[18,] NaN      Integer,0 NA    NA   <br>[19,] 22090.68 22087     21544 22645<br>[20,] NaN      Integer,0 NA    NA   <br>[21,] 30592.47 30587     29824 31371<br>[22,] 19477.45 19476     19214 19744<br>[23,] 15014.67 15014     14819 15212<br>[24,] 18168.45 18165     17677 18667<br>[25,] 10640.66 10640     10546 10737<br>[26,] 4301.43  4301      4221  4384 <br>[27,] NaN      Integer,0 NA    NA   <br>[28,] NaN      Integer,0 NA    NA   <br>[29,] NaN      Integer,0 NA    NA   <br>[30,] 22064.15 22058     21342 22799<br>[31,] 27397.54 27395     26941 27859<br>[32,] NaN      Integer,0 NA    NA   <br>[33,] 18584.7  18583     18263 18909<br>[34,] 17433.13 17432     17141 17728<br>[35,] 25166.49 25165     24812 25524<br>[